---
/**
 * routeup.dev landing page.
 * Structure: hero → problem strip → 01 daily workflow → 02 setup →
 *            03 recipes → public URL types → how it works → boundaries
 */
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>routeup | stable HTTPS names for local apps</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Give local apps stable, trusted HTTPS names. Keep your current dev command or let routeup run it, then expose the same targets publicly when needed."
    />
    <meta property="og:title" content="routeup | stable HTTPS names for local apps" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Use myapp.localhost instead of localhost:3000. Local by default, public only when you choose."
    />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://routeup.dev/" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="routeup" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://routeup.dev/og.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="routeup | stable HTTPS names for local apps" />
    <meta
      name="twitter:description"
      content="Use myapp.localhost instead of localhost:3000. Local by default, public only when you choose."
    />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://routeup.dev/og.png" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://routeup.dev/" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#e9e3d2" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <a href="#main-content" class="ru-skip">Skip to main content</a>
    <div role="status" class="ru-sr-live" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>

    <div class="ru-page">
      <header class="ru-nav">
        <a href="/" class="ru-brand" aria-label="routeup home">
          <img src="/favicon.svg" alt="" width="22" height="22" class="ru-brand__mark" />
          <span>routeup</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="ru-nav__links" aria-label="Primary">
          <a href="#workflows">Use routeup</a>
          <a href="#recipes">Recipes</a>
          <a href="#how">How it works</a>
          <a href="/docs">Docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/mukul-mehta/routeup" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="ru-nav__gh">GitHub &nearr;</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <main id="main-content">

        {/* ── HERO ── */}
        <section class="ru-hero">
          <div class="ru-hero__copy">
            <h1>Your local apps, by name.</h1>
            <p class="ru-hero__lede">
              Use <code>myapp.localhost</code> instead of <code>localhost:3000</code>.
              Keep running your app the way you already do, or let routeup start it and inject the URL.
              The route stays local unless you choose to expose it.
            </p>
            <div class="ru-ctas">
              <a href="#workflows" class="ru-btn ru-btn--primary">Choose your workflow</a>
              <a href="/docs/getting-started/install" class="ru-btn ru-btn--ghost">Install routeup</a>
            </div>
            <ul class="ru-proof" aria-label="Product guarantees">
              <li>No account for local routes</li>
              <li>Trusted local HTTPS</li>
              <li>Self-hostable server</li>
              <li>Open source</li>
              <li>Zero telemetry</li>
              <li>macOS and Linux</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="ru-hero__demo">
            <div class="ru-hero-modes" data-tabs>
              <div class="ru-hero-mode-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="routeup usage mode">
                <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="hero-serve" id="tab-hero-serve" data-tab-target="hero-serve">routeup serve</button>
                <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="hero-runner" id="tab-hero-runner" data-tab-target="hero-runner" tabindex="-1">routeup (runner)</button>
              </div>

              <div id="hero-serve" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-hero-serve" data-tab-panel="hero-serve" class="ru-hero-panel">
                <p class="ru-demo__context">Your app is already listening on port 3000</p>
                <div class="ru-code-wrap">
                  <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-hero-terminal" data-title="terminal"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup serve myapp --port 3000</span>

<span class="t-label">route:</span>   myapp
<span class="t-label">local:</span>   <span class="t-localurl">https://myapp.localhost</span>
<span class="t-label">targets:</span>
  /       http://localhost:3000

<span class="t-dim">press Ctrl-C to stop</span></code></pre>
                  <button class="ru-copy" type="button" data-copy="routeup serve myapp --port 3000" aria-label="Copy routeup serve command">Copy</button>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div id="hero-runner" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-hero-runner" data-tab-panel="hero-runner" class="ru-hero-panel" hidden>
                <p class="ru-demo__context">Let routeup pick the port and start your app</p>
                <div class="ru-code-stack">
                  <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="package.json"><code>{`{
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "routeup",
    "dev:app": "node server.mjs"
  },
  "routeup": {
    "name": "myapp",
    "script": "dev:app"
  }
}`}</code></pre>
                  <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="terminal"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">npm run dev</span>
<span class="t-dim">running: node server.mjs</span>

<span class="t-label">route:</span>   myapp
<span class="t-label">local:</span>   <span class="t-localurl">https://myapp.localhost</span></code></pre>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>


        </section>

        {/* ── 01 WORKFLOWS ── */}
        <section class="ru-section" id="workflows">
          <header class="ru-head">

            <h2>Two ways to use it. Same URL either way.</h2>
            <p>
              Route a port your app already listens on, or let routeup start the process and manage cleanup.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="ru-workflows" data-tabs>
            <div class="ru-workflow-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose how routeup runs">
              <button class="ru-workflow-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="workflow-existing" id="tab-workflow-existing" data-tab-target="workflow-existing">
                <span class="ru-choice__label">I already run my app</span>
                <span class="ru-choice__command">routeup serve</span>
                <span class="ru-choice__copy">Keep your current dev command and route its port.</span>
              </button>
              <button class="ru-workflow-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="workflow-runner" id="tab-workflow-runner" data-tab-target="workflow-runner" tabindex="-1">
                <span class="ru-choice__label">Let routeup run my app</span>
                <span class="ru-choice__command">routeup</span>
                <span class="ru-choice__copy">Assign a port, start the child process, and own cleanup.</span>
              </button>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-workflow-panel" id="workflow-existing" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-workflow-existing" data-tab-panel="workflow-existing">
              <div class="ru-workflow-panel__copy">
                <p class="ru-panel-tag">Best for fixed ports and existing tooling</p>
                <h3>Keep your app in one terminal. Route it in another.</h3>
                <p>
                  Nothing about your application command changes. Routeup registers the
                  name and proxies trusted HTTPS traffic to the port you provide.
                </p>
                <ol class="ru-steps">
                  <li><span>1</span>Start the app as usual.</li>
                  <li><span>2</span>Give its port a route name.</li>
                  <li><span>3</span>Open the stable HTTPS URL.</li>
                </ol>
                <a href="/docs/getting-started/first-route">Run your first route &rarr;</a>
              </div>
              <div class="ru-code-stack">
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="terminal 1"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">npm run dev</span>
<span class="t-dim">app listening on http://127.0.0.1:3000</span></code></pre>
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="terminal 2"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup serve myapp --port 3000</span>

<span class="t-label">route:</span>   myapp
<span class="t-label">local:</span>   <span class="t-localurl">https://myapp.localhost</span></code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-workflow-panel" id="workflow-runner" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-workflow-runner" data-tab-panel="workflow-runner" hidden>
              <div class="ru-workflow-panel__copy">
                <p class="ru-panel-tag">Best for the normal project dev command</p>
                <h3>Add the block once. Keep running <code>npm run dev</code>.</h3>
                <p>
                  Bare <code>routeup</code> picks a free port, registers the route before
                  launch, starts your script, and releases everything when the process exits.
                </p>
<a href="/docs/configuration/package-json-embed">package.json configuration &rarr;</a>
              </div>
              <div class="ru-code-stack">
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="package.json"><code>{`{
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "routeup",
    "dev:app": "node server.mjs"
  },
  "routeup": {
    "name": "myapp",
    "script": "dev:app"
  }
}`}</code></pre>
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="terminal"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">npm run dev</span>
<span class="t-dim">running: node server.mjs</span>

<span class="t-label">route:</span>   myapp
<span class="t-label">local:</span>   <span class="t-localurl">https://myapp.localhost</span></code></pre>
                <div class="ru-language-note">
                  <strong>Not using package.json?</strong>
                  <span>Put <code>{`"command": "go run ."`}</code> in <code>routeup.json</code>, then run <code>routeup</code>.</span>
                  <a href="/docs/configuration/frameworks">Check framework port setup &rarr;</a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── PROBLEM STRIP ── */}
        <section class="ru-problems" aria-label="Why routeup exists">
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="ru-problem__tag">[ports]</span>
              <p>Three services. Three ports to remember. One changes and the browser goes to the wrong app.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="ru-problem__tag">[tls]</span>
              <p>Secure cookies and HTTPS-only SDKs behave differently on <code>http://localhost</code>. The bugs show up after deploy.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="ru-problem__tag">[tunnel urls]</span>
              <p>Every ngrok session hands you a new random URL. Re-register it with Stripe or GitHub every morning.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="ru-problem__tag">[callbacks]</span>
              <p>OAuth providers want one redirect URI. Yours includes <code>localhost:3000</code> and breaks when the port changes.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        {/* ── 02 INSTALL ── */}
        <section class="ru-section ru-section--split" id="install">
          <header class="ru-section__intro">

            <h2>Trust the local CA once.</h2>
            <p>
              Install the single routeup binary, then run setup. It creates a local
              certificate authority, trusts it in your OS, prepares port 443, and
              starts the local agent.
            </p>
            <p class="ru-aside">
              Setup asks about a public server. Accept <code>https://edge.routeup.dev</code>
              if you want public routes later, or enter <code>none</code> for local-only use.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="ru-install" data-tabs>
            <div class="ru-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Install method">
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="install-brew" id="tab-install-brew" data-tab-target="install-brew">Homebrew</button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="install-curl" id="tab-install-curl" data-tab-target="install-curl" tabindex="-1">Install script</button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="install-release" id="tab-install-release" data-tab-target="install-release" tabindex="-1">Release</button>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-tab-panel" id="install-brew" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-install-brew" data-tab-panel="install-brew">
              <div class="ru-code-wrap">
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">brew install mukul-mehta/tap/routeup</span>
<span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup setup</span></code></pre>
                <button class="ru-copy" type="button" data-copy="brew install mukul-mehta/tap/routeup" aria-label="Copy Homebrew install command">Copy install</button>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-tab-panel" id="install-curl" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-install-curl" data-tab-panel="install-curl" hidden>
              <div class="ru-code-wrap">
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">curl -fsSL https://get.routeup.dev | sh</span>
<span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup setup</span></code></pre>
                <button class="ru-copy" type="button" data-copy="curl -fsSL https://get.routeup.dev | sh" aria-label="Copy install script command">Copy install</button>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-tab-panel ru-release" id="install-release" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-install-release" data-tab-panel="install-release" hidden>
              <p>Download a checksum-verified macOS or Linux binary from GitHub.</p>
              <a href="https://github.com/mukul-mehta/routeup/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open releases &nearr;</a>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-setup-result">
              <span>After setup</span>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>CA</strong> trusted by your OS</li>
                <li><strong>443</strong> ready for local HTTPS</li>
                <li><strong>Agent</strong> starts automatically when needed</li>
              </ul>
              <a href="/docs/getting-started/install">Installation details &rarr;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── 03 RECIPES ── */}
        <section class="ru-section" id="recipes">
          <header class="ru-head">

            <h2>Common tasks.</h2>
            <p>
              After your first route is running.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="ru-recipes" data-tabs>
            <div class="ru-recipe-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Routeup recipes">
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="recipe-compose" id="tab-recipe-compose" data-tab-target="recipe-compose">
                <span>01</span><strong>Frontend + API</strong><small>One origin, two targets</small>
              </button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="recipe-public" id="tab-recipe-public" data-tab-target="recipe-public" tabindex="-1">
                <span>02</span><strong>Share publicly</strong><small>Reuse an active route</small>
              </button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="recipe-webhook" id="tab-recipe-webhook" data-tab-target="recipe-webhook" tabindex="-1">
                <span>03</span><strong>Expose one path</strong><small>Keep the rest local</small>
              </button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="recipe-logs" id="tab-recipe-logs" data-tab-target="recipe-logs" tabindex="-1">
                <span>04</span><strong>Follow traffic</strong><small>Local and public logs</small>
              </button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="recipe-inspect" id="tab-recipe-inspect" data-tab-target="recipe-inspect" tabindex="-1">
                <span>05</span><strong>Inspect a request</strong><small>Opt-in capture</small>
              </button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="recipe-diagnose" id="tab-recipe-diagnose" data-tab-target="recipe-diagnose" tabindex="-1">
                <span>06</span><strong>Diagnose routes</strong><small>See owners and health</small>
              </button>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-recipe-panel" id="recipe-compose" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-recipe-compose" data-tab-panel="recipe-compose">
              <div class="ru-recipe-panel__copy">
                <p class="ru-panel-tag">Compose local services</p>
                <h3>Put the frontend and API behind one origin.</h3>
                <p>
                  Longest path prefix wins. The browser sees one HTTPS origin, so cookies
                  work across both targets and local CORS configuration disappears.
                </p>
                <dl>
                  <div><dt><code>/</code></dt><dd>Frontend on port 5173</dd></div>
                  <div><dt><code>/api</code></dt><dd>API on port 8080</dd></div>
                </dl>
                <a href="/docs/recipes/frontend-plus-api">Frontend + API recipe &rarr;</a>
              </div>
              <div class="ru-code-stack">
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="routeup.json"><code>{`{
  "name": "myapp",
  "targets": [
    { "path": "/", "port": 5173 },
    { "path": "/api", "port": 8080 }
  ]
}`}</code></pre>
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="terminal"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup serve</span>
<span class="t-localurl">https://myapp.localhost/</span>       &rarr; :5173
<span class="t-localurl">https://myapp.localhost/api</span>    &rarr; :8080</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-recipe-panel" id="recipe-public" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-recipe-public" data-tab-panel="recipe-public" hidden>
              <div class="ru-recipe-panel__copy">
                <p class="ru-panel-tag">Mobile testing and previews</p>
                <h3>Expose an already-running route from a second terminal.</h3>
                <p>
                  <code>routeup expose</code> reuses a route that is already active in another terminal —
                  your app keeps running unchanged. It exposes all paths. Use recipe 03 if you want to
                  limit which paths the public server forwards.
                </p>
                <p class="ru-warning">
                  A <code>try.routeup.dev</code> address is session-only and reachable by anyone who has
                  the URL. Routeup does not add viewer authentication in v1.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/getting-started/exposing-publicly">Public exposure guide &rarr;</a>
              </div>
              <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="terminal 2"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup expose</span>

<span class="t-label">route:</span>   myapp
<span class="t-label">local:</span>   <span class="t-localurl">https://myapp.localhost</span>
<span class="t-label">public:</span>  <span class="t-publicurl">https://myapp.try.routeup.dev</span>
<span class="t-label">expose:</span>  all paths

<span class="t-dim">press Ctrl-C to stop</span></code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-recipe-panel" id="recipe-webhook" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-recipe-webhook" data-tab-panel="recipe-webhook" hidden>
              <div class="ru-recipe-panel__copy">
                <p class="ru-panel-tag">Webhook development</p>
                <h3>Make the webhook handler public, not the whole app.</h3>
                <p>
                  <code>expose.paths</code> limits which paths the public server forwards. Local traffic
                  still reaches every target. Requests from the internet receive a 404 unless they match
                  the allowed prefix.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Setting <code>"enabled": true</code> in <code>expose</code> lets bare <code>routeup</code> (runner mode)
                  open the public tunnel automatically before your app starts, injecting the live public URL
                  into <code>ROUTEUP_URL</code>. For <code>routeup serve</code>, pass <code>--expose</code> instead and skip <code>enabled</code>.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/recipes/webhook-development">Webhook recipe &rarr;</a>
              </div>
              <div class="ru-code-stack">
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="routeup.json"><code>{`{
  "name": "myapp",
  "port": 8080,
  "expose": {
    "enabled": true,
    "paths": ["/api/webhooks/*"]
  }
}`}</code></pre>
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="terminal (runner mode)"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup</span>
<span class="t-label">route:</span>   myapp
<span class="t-label">local:</span>   <span class="t-localurl">https://myapp.localhost</span>
<span class="t-label">public:</span>  <span class="t-publicurl">https://myapp.try.routeup.dev</span>
<span class="t-label">expose:</span>  /api/webhooks/*</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-recipe-panel" id="recipe-logs" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-recipe-logs" data-tab-panel="recipe-logs" hidden>
              <div class="ru-recipe-panel__copy">
                <p class="ru-panel-tag">Request visibility</p>
                <h3>Follow local and public requests in one stream.</h3>
                <p>
                  Request logs include source, route, method, path, status, duration, and a
                  request ID. Headers and bodies are not retained unless capture is enabled.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/cli-reference/logs">Logs reference &rarr;</a>
              </div>
              <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat ru-terminal--wide" data-title="terminal"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup logs myapp --follow</span>

<span class="t-dim">TIME      SOURCE  METHOD  PATH                  STATUS  ID</span>
14:02:01  local   GET     /api/users            <span class="t-ok">200</span>  req_Kx4mT9pL2aQ7vN6cR
14:02:03  public  POST    /api/webhooks/stripe  <span class="t-ok">204</span>  req_Jz6nR2wL8cP4sD9h</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-recipe-panel" id="recipe-inspect" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-recipe-inspect" data-tab-panel="recipe-inspect" hidden>
              <div class="ru-recipe-panel__copy">
                <p class="ru-panel-tag">Opt-in request capture</p>
                <h3>Capture deliberately, redact secrets, then inspect.</h3>
                <p>
                  Capture is off by default. Enable request or response capture per route and
                  list every sensitive header that should not be retained.
                </p>
                <p class="ru-warning">Captured data stays in the local agent's bounded in-memory buffer and is cleared on restart.</p>
                <a href="/docs/cli-reference/inspect">Inspect reference &rarr;</a>
              </div>
              <div class="ru-code-stack">
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="routeup.json"><code>{`{
  "capture": {
    "request": true,
    "response": true,
    "redact_headers": [
      "authorization",
      "cookie",
      "x-webhook-signature"
    ]
  }
}`}</code></pre>
                <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat" data-title="terminal"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup inspect req_Jz6nR2wL8cP4sD9h</span>
<span class="t-label">Source:</span>  public
<span class="t-label">Method:</span>  POST
<span class="t-label">Path:</span>    /api/webhooks/stripe
<span class="t-label">Capture:</span> complete</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ru-recipe-panel" id="recipe-diagnose" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-recipe-diagnose" data-tab-panel="recipe-diagnose" hidden>
              <div class="ru-recipe-panel__copy">
                <p class="ru-panel-tag">Route ownership and setup health</p>
                <h3>See what is active before changing anything.</h3>
                <p>
                  <code>routeup routes</code> identifies every active name, target, public URL,
                  owner PID, age, and working directory. <code>routeup doctor</code> checks the
                  CA, trust store, port 443, and agent.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/cli-reference/routes">Routes reference &rarr;</a>
              </div>
              <pre translate="no" class="ru-terminal ru-terminal--flat ru-terminal--wide" data-title="terminal"><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup routes</span>
<span class="t-dim">NAME    TARGETS  PUBLIC  PID    CWD</span>
myapp   /:3000   -       48172  ~/code/myapp

<span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">routeup doctor</span>
<span class="t-ok">ok</span>  certificate authority
<span class="t-ok">ok</span>  system trust
<span class="t-ok">ok</span>  port 443</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── PUBLIC URL TYPES ── */}
        <section class="ru-section" id="public">
          <header class="ru-head ru-head--narrow">
            <p class="ru-kicker">URL types</p>
            <h2>Local and public routes have different lifetimes.</h2>
            <p>
              A route name, a public address, and a running process expire independently.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="ru-lifetimes">
            <article>
              <p class="ru-lifetime__label ru-lifetime__label--local">Local</p>
              <h3><code>myapp.localhost</code></h3>
              <p>Stable on your machine. No account, token, public server, DNS, or network connection.</p>
              <strong>Available while the owning command runs</strong>
            </article>
            <article>
              <p class="ru-lifetime__label ru-lifetime__label--try">Try public</p>
              <h3><code>myapp.try.routeup.dev</code></h3>
              <p>Token-less and internet-accessible. The claim is session-only and can be taken again after disconnect.</p>
              <strong>For previews, webhooks, and mobile tests</strong>
            </article>
            <article>
              <p class="ru-lifetime__label ru-lifetime__label--named">Named public</p>
              <h3><code>myapp.mukul.routeup.dev</code></h3>
              <p>A reusable address authorized by an operator-issued namespace token. The app is still offline when no tunnel is connected.</p>
              <strong>For OAuth callbacks and repeat integrations</strong>
            </article>
            <article>
              <p class="ru-lifetime__label ru-lifetime__label--self">Self-hosted</p>
              <h3><code>myapp.dev.example.com</code></h3>
              <p>Run the same routeup binary as your public server and control the domain, TLS, tokens, and namespace policy.</p>
              <a href="/docs/self-hosting/running-the-server">Self-hosting guide &rarr;</a>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── HOW IT WORKS ── */}
        <section class="ru-section" id="how">
          <header class="ru-head ru-head--narrow">
            <p class="ru-kicker">How it works</p>
            <h2>The same local target, two paths to reach it.</h2>
            <p>
              Local requests never leave your machine. Public requests reach a routeup
              server first, then travel through an outbound encrypted tunnel. Your app
              keeps listening on loopback in both cases.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="ru-flows">
            <article class="ru-flow">
              <div class="ru-flow__header"><span class="ru-status ru-status--local"></span><strong>Local request</strong><small>No server contact</small></div>
              <ol>
                <li><span>Browser</span><code>https://myapp.localhost</code></li>
                <li><span>Local agent</span><small>terminates trusted TLS</small></li>
                <li><span>Your app</span><code>127.0.0.1:3000</code></li>
              </ol>
            </article>
            <article class="ru-flow ru-flow--public">
              <div class="ru-flow__header"><span class="ru-status ru-status--public"></span><strong>Public request</strong><small>Only when exposed</small></div>
              <ol>
                <li><span>Internet client</span><code>https://myapp.try.routeup.dev</code></li>
                <li><span>Routeup server</span><small>terminates public TLS</small></li>
                <li><span>Outbound tunnel</span><small>encrypted back to your agent</small></li>
                <li><span>Your app</span><code>127.0.0.1:3000</code></li>
              </ol>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── BOUNDARIES ── */}
        <section class="ru-section ru-section--split ru-section--last">
          <header class="ru-section__intro">
            <p class="ru-kicker">The boundaries</p>
            <h2>One binary. No hidden platform.</h2>
            <p>
              The CLI, local agent, and public server are one Go binary. Local use is
              offline-capable and sends no telemetry. Public exposure is optional and
              can point at the hosted server or your own deployment.
            </p>
            <div class="ru-ctas">
              <a href="/docs" class="ru-btn ru-btn--primary">Read the docs</a>
              <a href="https://github.com/mukul-mehta/routeup" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="ru-btn ru-btn--ghost">View source &nearr;</a>
            </div>
          </header>
          <ul class="ru-boundaries">
            <li><strong>Local means local</strong><span>No account, token, DNS, or server request for <code>*.localhost</code>.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Capture is opt-in</strong><span>Request bodies are not retained unless a route explicitly enables capture.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Foreground owns lifetime</strong><span>Ctrl-C releases the route, child process, and tunnel owned by that command.</span></li>
            <li><strong>No hidden platform</strong><span>MIT licensed, zero telemetry, and self-hostable with documented server operations.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

      </main>

